        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fda9d626-0bae-5c68-9572-9c1c3fa4f3cd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leon Uris\n- Products: Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin, Exodus, Trinity\n- Places: Berlin, Germany, East Berlin, East Germany\n- Events: World War II, Berlin Airlift\n- Organizations: Western Allies, Soviet occupiers\n- Topics: historical fiction\n\nFacts:\n- Leon Marcus Uris was born on August 3, 1924, and he became an American author known for historical fiction.\n- Armageddon, also titled Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin, is a novel by Leon Uris about post-World War II Berlin and Germany.\n- Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin vividly describes the Berlin Airlift and the interactions among people of five nations, including the three major Western Allies and the Soviet occupiers of East Berlin and East Germany.\n- Leon Uris published the bestselling book Exodus in 1958.\n- Leon Uris published the bestselling book Trinity in 1976.\n- Leon Marcus Uris died on June 21, 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
